{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774719,"nonce":"rsWNzG+rqexEIzfEaJChmr4nX9k=","title":"feat(placement): ADR-0055 placement profiles — baseline + node pools + resources + governed k8s_overlay","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #34 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/adr-0055-placement-profiles` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-18T19:57:24Z · Merged: 2026-07-18T19:59:26Z\n\nImplements **ADR-0055** (finishes the never-built ADR-0026 and refines it). Motivated by dogfooding Scarab on Acme's tainted, multi-pool cluster — the exact scheduling gaps that made Woodpecker painful.\n\n`runs_on`/`resources` existed in the pipeline schema but were **dropped at compile** — nothing reached the Pod, which had no `nodeSelector`/`tolerations`/`resources`. So Scarab step Pods were **unschedulable** on a tainted cluster.\n\n- **Baseline** (operator config): the control plane stamps default tolerations/nodeSelector/resources onto *every* step Pod — no Kyverno/MutatingAdmissionPolicy backstop needed (Scarab builds the Pod directly). This is the Acme pain-killer.\n- **PlacementProfiles**: an admin-owned registry (`placement_profiles`, gitops YAML via `SCARAB_PLACEMENT_CONFIG_FILE`). Each profile is an opaque k8s overlay. A job names one or more (`placement_profiles: [arm64, critical]`), merged in listed order — no cluster names or k8s in pipelines beyond the profile name.\n- **`resources: {cpu_millis, memory_mib}`** — exact specifics applied to the step container (Guaranteed QoS). No `size` tiers.\n- **`k8s_overlay`** — the rare raw escape hatch, **governed \u0026 fail-closed** like ADR-0039 grants: honored only under an Environment with `permit_k8s_overlay` set, else the run is rejected.\n\nMerge order: `baseline → named profiles (listed order) → resources → k8s_overlay (if granted)`.\n\n- `scarab-pipeline`: `placement_profiles` (replaces stubbed `runs_on`), `resources`, `k8s_overlay` + validation.\n- `scarab-engine`: fields carried on the persisted StepSpec (survive resume).\n- `scarab-server`: IR→StepSpec plumbing (3 sites); `admit_k8s_overlay` governance; `SCARAB_PLACEMENT_CONFIG_FILE` (fail-closed boot).\n- `scarab-executor-k8s`: `PlacementConfig` + `apply_placement` (baseline/profile/resource/overlay merge); unknown profile fails closed. Applied to step **and** debug pods.\n- `scarab-project`: `permit_k8s_overlay` on ProtectionRules.\n- Docs: ADR-0055, CONTEXT.md glossary, ADR index; regenerated `openapi.json`.\n\nAll unit suites green: pipeline (+3), executor (+8 apply_placement: baseline stamp, profile-merge order, Guaranteed-QoS resources, default fallback, **unknown-profile fail-closed**, overlay-wins-last, no-op preservation), server-lib (+4 overlay admission). Integration tests (Postgres/kind) not run in this PR — unit-level only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}